{
  "run_id": "20260903-114606-phase0_refactor_check",
  "experiment": {
    "name": "phase0_refactor_check",
    "description": [
      "Regression check on the sampler/victim-pool extraction (util/sampler.c,",
      "util/victim-pool.c). The driver's measurement loop moved out of",
      "src/driver.c into shared modules so the covert-channel receiver could use",
      "the same instrument rather than a copy of it. The move was mechanical, but",
      "every Phase 0 and Phase 1 number depends on that loop, so it gets a",
      "measurement, not an assurance.",
      "",
      "The anchor is the check that matters: ws_l3_x8 with selectors [0, 2^32-1]",
      "at these exact driver settings has read +1.841, +1.904, +1.943 and +2.054 W",
      "in four earlier sessions. A result inside that range means the extracted",
      "sampler measures what the inline one did. The A/A confirms the rebuilt path",
      "still cannot manufacture an effect."
    ],
